<h1>Aging in Incarceration: Age at Conviction vs. Current Age</h1>

<p>Prisoners are rotting away in their jail cells.</p>

<p>Do prisoners' lifespan not matter anymore? Are they supposed to rot away in their jail cells for the rest of their life? Multiple prisoners data has been collected regarding their age at conviction and their most up to date. Most prisoners regardless of age and gender have been in prison for a minimum of 10 years. Some have even been in prison for more than half of their age. The large difference between the age at conviction to their current age questions the process of sentencing prisoners and whether their sentence will uphold in the passing of years.</p>

